=== screen help ===
                                            LithicRivers
┌Help──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│Controls                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                  │
│On the World page, h shows or hides context help: the keys for what you're doing now.             │
│                                                                                                  │
│Factory blocks (chests, wooden conveyors): place them in Place mode, where r turns the next one;  │
│Rotate mode turns placed ones. f opens a chest, or puts the selected inventory item on an empty   │
│belt. Belts carry items into whatever they face. Power: burner generators burn logs, planks,      │
│sticks or shavings; power poles link within 8 tiles and power blocks within 3. Auto-planters plant│
│acorns and auto-harvesters chop grown trees within 2 tiles, pushing the wood into what they face. │
│Crude furnaces smelt wood into biochar, a denser fuel: items from the back go in, fuel comes from │
│the sides, and biochar leaves the front. Electric furnaces smelt the same on grid power, taking   │
│items from the back and both sides. Extractors move one item a second from the block behind them  │
│into the block in front; filter extractors and belt routers take a filter (interact to set it).   │
│Routers deal items left, straight and right in turn, or send the filtered item left. You can walk │
│on belts, and they carry you along. , lets 10 game seconds pass.                                  │
│                                                                                                  │
│Mouse: left click opens what's there, else places the hotbar block; right click breaks; middle    │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
